G'), ('2005', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2007', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2008', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2009', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2010', 'Atlético-GO'), ('2010', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2011', 'Atlético-GO'), ('2011', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2012', 'Atlético-GO'), ('2012', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2013', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2014', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2015', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2016', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2017', 'Atlético-GO'), ('2017', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2018', 'Atlético-MG'), ('2019', 'Atlético-MG')]\nFIFA clubs with Brazilians (top 40): [('Grêmio', 20), ('Atlético Mineiro', 20), ('Cruzeiro', 20), ('Fluminense', 20), ('Santos', 20), ('Internacional', 20), ('América FC (Minas Gerais)', 20), ('Botafogo', 20), ('Bahia', 20), ('Paraná', 20), ('Atlético Paranaense', 20), ('Vitória', 20), ('Sport Club do Recife', 20), ('Chapecoense', 20), ('Ceará Sporting Club', 20), ('Portimonense SC', 18), ('SC Braga', 13), ('CD Aves', 12), ('Rio Ave FC', 12), ('Clube Sport Marítimo', 10), ('GD Chaves', 10), ('Shakhtar Donetsk', 9), ('FC Porto', 8), ('Boavista FC', 8), ('Santa Clara', 8), ('CD Feirense', 7), ('CD Nacional', 7), ('Moreirense FC', 7), ('Sporting CP', 6), ('FC Nantes', 6), ('Vitória Guimarães', 6), ('LOSC Lille', 5), ('Al Wehda', 5), ('Vitória de Setúbal', 5), ('Al Batin', 5), ('Paris Saint-Germain', 4), ('FC Barcelona', 4), ('Manchester City', 4), ('Guangzhou Evergrande Taobao FC', 4), ('Querétaro', 4)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, unicodedata, collections\nbase='data/kaggle/'\ndef fold(s):\n    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', s)\n    s = ''.join(ch for ch in s if not unicodedata.combining(ch))\n    return re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]', '', s.lower())\n\nnames = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    names[r['home_team']] += 1; names[r['away_team']] += 1\ncup = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    cup[r['home_team']] += 1; cup[r['away_team']] += 1\nnovo = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    novo[r['Equipe_mandante']] += 1; novo[r['Equipe_visitante']] += 1\nbrf = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    brf[r['home']] += 1; brf[r['away']] += 1\n\n# strip suffixes, find collisions after stripping\ndef strip_suffix(n):\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s*\\([^)]*\\)', '', n)  # parenthetical\n    n = re.sub(r'\\s*-\\s*[A-Z]{2}$', '', n)  # \" - RJ\" or \"-RJ\"\n    return n.strip()\nbases = collections.defaultdict(set)\nfor src, ctr in [('br', names), ('cup', cup), ('novo', novo), ('brf', brf)]:\n    for n in ctr:\n        bases[fold(strip_suffix(n))].add((n, src))\ncoll = {b: v for b, v in bases.items() if len(v) > 1}\nprint('collisions after stripping suffixes:')\nfor b, v in sorted(coll.items()): print(' ', b, '->', sorted(v))\n\n# how many distinct names total\nprint('distinct names: br=%d cup=%d novo=%d brf=%d' % (len(names), len(cup), len(novo), len(brf)))\n\n# novo: atletico-pr naming over years\nat = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    for c in ('Equipe_mandante','Equipe_visitante'):\n        if 'tl' in r[c]: at[(r['Ano'], r[c])] += 1\nprint('novo atletico variants by year:', sorted({(y, n) for (y, n) in at}))\n\n# FIFA brazilian clubs\nclubs = collections.Counter()\nnat_br = collections.Counter()\nfor r in csv.DictReader(open(base+'fifa_data.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')):\n    if r['Nationality'] == 'Brazil':\n        clubs[r['Club']] += 1\nprint('FIFA clubs with Brazilians (top 40):', clubs.most_common(40))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788241140638,"end":1788241140640}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"With numeric conversion: of 1353 same-key overlaps, 1325 agree directly (97.9%). So BR-Football is NOT swapped — the earlier disagreement was my string comparison. The 28 disagreements are likely data errors in one source or edge cases.\n\nSo the plan for dedup:\n- Competition \"brasileirao\" (Serie A): sources = novo (2003-2019), Brasileirao_Matches (2012-2022), BR-Football Serie A (2014-2023). Overlapping seasons 2014-2022 across all three. Dedup preference: Brasileirao_Matches (richest: datetime, state, round) > novo (has stadium, round) > BR-Foot (has stats).\n- Dedup key: (season, round, home_key, away_key) — novo and Brasileirao agreed on rounds for all 1924 common keys. BR-Foot has no round... it has date though. For BR-Foot rows, I can dedup by (season, home_key, away_key) since a pair meets at most twice... wait, in Serie A each pair meets twice (home and away), so (season, home, away) is unique per fixture. 1353 same-key overlaps out of... BR-Foot Serie A 2014-2022 portion. Each (season, home_key, away_key) fixture appears once per source, so dedup by (season, home_key, away_key, competition) is sufficient!\n\nThat's the right dedup key: **(competition, season, home_key, away_key)**. Each source lists a given fixture once. For cup/libertadores, teams can meet multiple times in same season (e.g., two-legged finals with same home team? rare but possible — e.g., Copa do Brasil two legs: home team in leg 1 is away in leg 2, but if both legs at same home stadium... possible). To be safe, key = (competition, season, home_key, away_key, date). But dates differ between sources? novo date (29/03/2003) vs Brasileirao datetime same day presumably. BR-Foot date is ISO too. Hmm, for the dedup between novo/Brasileirao/BR-Foot on Serie A, (season, home, away) suffices since round-robin ensures exactly one fixture per (home, away) pair per season — actually in a double round-robin, pair (A home, B away) occurs exactly once per season. True for Serie A. For cups it can occur more (two legs same venue). But cups: Brazilian_Cup_Matches vs BR-Foot 'Copa do Brasil' both cover 2014-2023! Also overlapping! Both would have the same fixtures with dates. For cups I'll dedup by (competition, season, home_key, away_key, date, round/stage) — combining.\n\nActually, simpler and safer approach: treat each source as distinct \"source\" but dedupe only the known overlapping Serie A fixtures (novo + BR-Foot vs Brasileirao_Matches), and for Copa do Brasil dedupe BR-Foot vs Brazilian_Cup_Matches by (season, date, home, away). Since the spec examples rarely hinge on this, but data quality matters (\"Cross-file queries work\"), dedup matters for standings correctness (double-counting would corrupt standings).\n\nLet me check BR-Foot Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup_Matches overlap with numeric goals.\n\nAlso Libertadores: only one source (Libertadores_Matches.csv). Fine.\n\nAlso need to check: does BR-Foot Serie A 2023 give us the 2023 season (Brasileirao_Matches ends 2022)? Yes — 2023-12-07. So \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" can be answered via BR-Foot + Copa do Brasil file (2023? cup ends 2023-09-24 — yes! The final São Paulo vs Flamengo 2023-09-24 is in BR-Foot. Wait, does Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv include 2023? Earlier seasons showed 2012-2021 (last: ('2021', 108)). So Cup file: 2012-2021, BR-Foot Copa do Brasil: 2014-2023.\n\nLet me check BR-Foot Copa overlap vs Cup file, and confirm which seasons each source covers for copa. Also sample FIFA club names for Brazilian clubs to plan player-club queries. And check the 28 Serie A disagreements - just note as data-quality noise; choose Brasileirao_Matches as authoritative.\n\nAlso check Athletico-PR vs Atlético-PR naming (novo has \"Athletico-PR\" from 2019?, \"Atlético-PR\" earlier?). And Atlético-MG in cup file (\"América - MG\" pattern with \" - \"). Team key folding: strip \"-XX\" suffix where XX is a state code. Need list of valid state abbreviations to avoid stripping e.g. \"CSA\"? \"CSA\" has no dash, fine. But careful with names like \"Barcelona-EQU\" (country code), \"Nacional (URU)\" in Libertadores — strip country suffixes too. And in the Cup file: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → remove parenthetical, strip \" - RJ\" → \"Boavista Sport Club\" → fold → \"boavistasportclub\" — matching by substring \"boavista\" would work.\n\nMatching strategy for user queries: fold to key; try exact match against known keys; then substring/startswith match; then alias table for common cases (\"Atletico-MG\" → \"atleticomg\"... wait if I strip state suffixes, \"Atlético-PR\" → \"atleticopr\" → strip → \"atletico\". But there's also \"Atlético-GO\" (Atlético Goianiense)! Stripping \"-GO\" → \"atletico\" would COLLIDE Atlético-PR with Atlético-GO. Danger!\n\nSo I can't blindly strip state suffixes. Better: key = fold(name) with state suffix REMOVED only when it creates no collision... that's complex. Alternative: keep the state as part of identity but maintain alias mapping: canonical_name = name with suffix (e.g., \"Atlético-PR\", \"Atlético-GO\"). For matching a user query \"atletico-pr\" or \"athletico\" or \"atlético paranaense\": \n1. fold query\n2. exact key match (key includes suffix-stripped base + state if known?)\n\nLet me inventory the actual distinct team names across all match files to see collision risk. Names like \"Athletico-PR\" (novo 2019+) vs \"Atlético-PR\" (novo 2003-2018?) vs BR-Foot \"Athletico-PR\"? Let me collect.\n\nAlso FIFA clubs: check which Brazilian clubs appear (e.g., \"Grêmio\", \"Flamengo\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo\", \"Atlético-MG\"?). FIFA 19-era data (2018?). Let me check.\n\nThen design the TeamRegistry:\n- alias → canonical (e.g., from all observed variants: strip state suffix where unambiguous, plus manual aliases: \"atletico\" ambiguous → don't map).\n- Query resolution: exact fold match on any alias → canonical; else unique substring match across aliases; if multiple matches → return them (disambiguation message); if none → fuzzy via difflib get_close_matches.\n\nCollision check needed: after stripping state suffixes, which bases collide? (\"Atlético-MG\"/\"Atlético-PR\"/\"Atlético-GO\" → \"atletico\" ×3; \"América-MG\"/\"América-RN\"/\"América-SC\"? etc.) For those, canonical stays suffixed and \"atletico\" alone maps to multiple → ambiguous. But \"atleticopr\" maps fine. And common queries like \"Athletico\" → user probably means Atlético-PR; I'll report ambiguity listing candidates.\n\nLet me gather the full team name inventory now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b7a3f3c001AcE9fZ7zL0wLj8","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b79cedc001Rcw3xIenrV5Wcp"}}
