)\nprint('brazilian positions:', pos.most_common())\nEOF","time":{"start":1788241194372,"end":1788241194375}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a full picture. Key design decisions:\n\n**Team name normalization:**\n- State suffix collisions exist (Atlético-MG/PR/GO/AC/BA/ES, América-MG/RN, Botafogo-RJ/PB, etc.). So the normalized key should KEEP the state when present. Canonical display: e.g. \"Atlético-MG\". But Brasileirao_Matches uses \"Atletico-MG\" (no accent), novo \"Atlético-MG\" — fold() handles accent-insensitivity so key = fold(\"Atlético-MG\") = \"atleticomg\". \n\n- Key format: fold of name with parentheticals removed, state suffix normalized to \"-XX\" form (no spaces). So \"América - MG\" → \"americamg\", \"Atletico Mineiro\" (BR-Foot/FIFA) → \"atleticomineiro\" ≠ \"atleticomg\"! BR-Foot calls it \"Atletico Mineiro\"; cup file calls it \"Atlético Mineiro - MG\". And FIFA \"Atlético Mineiro\". So I need alias mapping: atleticomineiro → atleticomg. Similarly \"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Atletico Paranaense\" → atleticopr; \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → vascodagamarj; \"Sport Club do Recife\" (FIFA) → sportpe; \"Ceará Sporting Club\" (FIFA) → cearace; \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" (FIFA) → americamg.\n\nSo: canonical key = base+state (e.g. \"atleticomg\"), and I maintain an alias table mapping state-less keys and special full names to canonical keys. For aliases like \"atletico\" (ambiguous), don't resolve — require more specific query OR list candidates.\n\nApproach for registry:\n1. For each raw name: clean = remove parentheticals (\"(antigo ...)\", \"(URU)\", \"(PI)\"), collapse \" - XX\" → \"-XX\", strip accents → key_raw.\n2. State-suffixed key: if matches r'-([A-Z]{2})$' → canonical \"base-UF\" key e.g. fold(\"Atlético-MG\")=\"atleticomg\".\n3. Alias map: stateless base key (\"atleticomineiro\"? no...) Let me define:\n   - If name has state suffix → canonical key = fold(base)+'-'+uf.lower() e.g. \"atlet