 → ceara-ce (alias). \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → remove parenthetical → \"América FC\" → base \"americafc\"? fold → \"americafc\" — needs alias americafc → america-mg. Hmm, \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" — strip parens → \"América FC\" → fold \"americafc\". Add alias: \"americafc\" → \"america-mg\". OK.\n\nAlso FIFA has \"Botafogo\" (stateless) → ambiguous botafogo-rj/pb → in FIFA context, Botafogo = Botafogo-RJ (Serie A club) → resolve by majority. \"Bahia\" → bahia-ba unique ✓. \"Paraná\" → parana-pr unique ✓. \"Vitória\" → vitoria-ba unique (Vitória da Conquista is different base \"vitoriadaconquista\") ✓. \"Chapecoense\" → chapecoense-sc ✓. \"Santos\" → ambiguous santos-sp/santos-ap → majority → santos-sp ✓. \"Internacional\" → inter-rs/inter-sc → majority → internacional-rs ✓. \"Cruzeiro\" → cruzeiro-mg ✓. \"Fluminense\" → fluminense-rj ✓.\n\nMajority resolution is right for FIFA + BR-Foot Serie A/B/C? For BR-Foot Serie C \"Botafogo\" → majority picks RJ — wrong for PB. Let me check how much this matters: does Botafogo-PB appear in BR-Foot Serie C as \"Botafogo\"? Botafogo-PB played Serie C in 2015? and Serie B 2016-2019. Botafogo-RJ played Serie A 2016-2020 (relegated after 2020), Serie B 2021, back to Serie A 2022-23. So Serie B 2016-2019: \"Botafogo\" = PB (RJ was in Serie A those years!). Majority heuristic FAILS here (RJ has more total matches historically). Serie B 2021: \"Botafogo\" = RJ.\n\nSo for BR-Foot I DO need per-(tournament, season) disambiguation. Context signal: which canonical candidate played in a *different tournament the same season*? E.g., Serie B 2016 \"Botafogo\": RJ played Serie A 2016 (from br file, suffixed!). So in season 2016, \"Botafogo\" in Serie B must be PB (since RJ is in Serie A 2016). That's a clean rule:\n\n**Coexistence rule**: when resolving a stateless name in (tournament T, season S): candidates from suffixed sources that appear in a DIFFERENT competition in season S are excluded (a club plays one national division per season). If one candidate remains → resolved. If zero or multiple remain → majority by total historical match count. Exception: Copa do Brasil runs parallel to leagues — a club plays copa AND serie A same season. So the exclusion only applies between LEAGUES (serie a/b/c mutually exclusive), not copa/libertadores. BR-Foot tournaments: Serie A/B/C are leagues (mutually exclusive per season); Copa do Brasil parallel. So rule applies within league family. For copa context: can't use exclusion → majority. But copa has suffixed sources (cup file) covering 2012-2021; BR-Foot copa is 2014-2023. For overlapping (pair, season) dedup between cup file and BR-Foot copa I need matching names anyway...\n\nHmm wait, actually — do I even need to merge BR-Foot Copa do Brasil with the cup file? The cup file (2012-2021, has state suffixes + rounds) vs BR-Foot copa (2014-2023, has stats: corners/shots). Merging: for seasons 2012-2013, only cup file. 2022-2023, only BR-Foot. 2014-2021, both. If I merge with dedup, I get richest rows (cup file structure + BR-Foot stats where joinable). Joining on (pair, season, date) — the date must match exactly; BR-Foot dates might differ (e.g., a match postponed...). Earlier with WRONG keys I got 217 common with 56 agreement — that was garbage because keys mismatched. Let me re-check the join properly: strip suffixes from BOTH sides for the join key (base+base+season+date) and see agreement. If dates align, great; otherwise join on (pair, season, date±1)? Let me test.\n\nAlso for the Brasileirão merge — 3 sources. br_matches 2012-2022 (suffixed, rounds, datetime). novo 2003-2019 (suffixed, stadium, round). BR-Foot serie A 2014-2023 (stateless, stats). Merge: base = br_matches rows for 2012-2022; novo for 2003-2011; BR-Foot for 2023 + enrich overlapping rows with stats.\n\nFor enrichment join (BR-Foot stats onto merged matches): key = (home_base, away_base, season, date)? br_matches datetime date vs BR-Foot date. novo Data (d/m/Y). Join tolerance: exact date first; fallback (pair, season) if unique.\n\nLet me now verify: (a) cup join by base+season+date; (b) serie A join br_matches↔BR-Foot by base+season+date agreement; (c) per-season ambiguous bases in BR-Foot leagues — which cases exist; (d) cup per-season final rounds; (e) libertadores final per season (two-legged vs single).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b7bffeb001n3jwSO61BW0KdP","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b7b2ece0010lgaSu1OmjbBBc"}}
