{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788241884989,"sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-81b6533ee3ddf4ad","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, collections\nlib = list(csv.DictReader(open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')))\nnames = collections.Counter()\nfor r in lib:\n    names[r['home_team']] += 1; names[r['away_team']] += 1\nbrz = {n:c for n,c in names.items() if n in (\n 'Flamengo','Athletico','Atletico','Palmeiras','Santos','Gremio','Corinthians','Sao Paulo','Vasco',\n 'Fluminense','Botafogo','Atletico-MG','Atletico-PR','Internacional','Cruzeiro','Gremio-RS','Atletico Mineiro')}\nprint('bare/known BR names in lib:', {n:c for n,c in names.items() if any(n.startswith(x) for x in ('Flamengo','Athletico','Atletico','Palmeiras','Santos','Gremio','Corinthians','Sao Paulo','Vasco','Fluminense','Botafogo','Internacional','Cruzeiro'))})\nEOF"},"output":"bare/known BR names in lib: {'Palmeiras': 81, 'Corinthians': 42, 'Fluminense': 20, 'Botafogo': 16, 'Cruzeiro': 38, 'Flamengo': 66, 'Santos Laguna': 8, 'Internacional': 38, 'Santos': 37, 'Vasco': 6, 'Athletico': 29}\n","metadata":{"output":"bare/known BR names in lib: {'Palmeiras': 81, 'Corinthians': 42, 'Fluminense': 20, 'Botafogo': 16, 'Cruzeiro': 38, 'Flamengo': 66, 'Santos Laguna': 8, 'Internacional': 38, 'Santos': 37, 'Vasco': 6, 'Athletico': 29}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, re, collections\nlib = list(csv.DictReader(open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig')))\nnames = collections.Counter()\nfor r in lib:\n    names[r['home_team']] += 1; names[r['away_team']] += 1\nbrz = {n:c for n,c in names.items() if n in (\n 'Flamengo','Athletico','Atletico','Palmeiras','Santos','Gremio','Corinthians','Sao Paulo','Vasco',\n 'Fluminense','Botafogo','Atletico-MG','Atletico-PR','Internacional','Cruzeiro','Gremio-RS','Atletico Mineiro')}\nprint('bare/known BR names in lib:', {n:c for n,c in names.items() if any(n.startswith(x) for x in ('Flamengo','Athletico','Atletico','Palmeiras','Santos','Gremio','Corinthians','Sao Paulo','Vasco','Fluminense','Botafogo','Internacional','Cruzeiro'))})\nEOF","time":{"start":1788241884984,"end":1788241884987}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the loader — the heart of the system. Let me carefully design it:\n\n```python\nclass SoccerData:\n    def __init__(self, data_dir='data/kaggle'):\n        self.registry = TeamRegistry()\n        self.matches: list[Match] = []\n        self.players: list[Player] = []\n        self._load_matches()\n        self._load_players()\n```\n\nLoading order for the registry to work:\n1. **Pass 1 (suffixed sources)**: register names from br_matches (suffixed), novo (state via UF columns), cup (suffixed), libertadores (mixed), BR-Foot suffixed names (\"Botafogo RJ\"). But I also need to CREATE Match objects in the same pass. The problem: BR-Foot stateless rows need coexistence info, which requires all league participation from suffixed sources — i.e., process br & novo first, then cup & lib, then BR-Foot.\n\nOrder:\na) Load br_matches → matches + register (suffixed, count appearance).\nb) Load novo → register w/ state_hint (count), dedupe vs existing brasileirao fixtures by (season, home_key, away_key); add new ones.\nc) Load cup file → register (suffixed, count); add matches (copa_do_brasil). Round labels: \"Round N\". Track (pair,season) → matches for later merge.\nd) Load libertadores → register (mostly suffixed/foreign); add matches. Fixup NA final → 2022.\ne) Load BR-Foot: for each row:\n   - tournament → competition (Serie A→brasileirao, Serie B→serie_b, Serie C→serie_c, Copa do Brasil→copa_do_brasil)\n   - register team names: suffixed (\"Botafogo RJ\") counted; stateless: resolve via alias→unique-base→coexistence→majority, NOT counted (to avoid skewing dominan