xtures with NA goals: 2022 rounds 29-38 (81) + 2016 (1) — kept, later filled by BR-Foot where available.\n\nnovo rows: skip if (comp='brasileirao', season, home_key, away_key) exists; else add with venue=Arena, round_label=f\"Round {Rodada}\", date=parse (Data), Vencedor unused (validate?). register with state_hint=Mandante_UF/Visitante_UF.\n\ncup rows: competition 'copa_do_brasil'; round_label = f\"Round {round}\". Keep NA rows (2021 round 4) — they'll be filled by BR-Foot where available. Register names (suffixed).\nAlso compute later (in service) per-season final round from played cup-file matches.\n\nlib rows: competition 'libertadores'; stage = stage.title() → \"Group Stage\", \"Round Of 16\"... hmm \"Round of 16\".title() → \"Round Of 16\" (wrong). Map manually: {'group stage': 'Group Stage', 'round of 16': 'Round of 16', 'quarterfinals': 'Quarterfinals', 'semifinals': 'Semifinals', 'final': 'Final'}.\nFixup: row with season NA & stage final → season=2022 (inferred), note.\n\nBR-Foot rows: \n- competition mapping: 'Serie A'→'brasileirao', 'Serie B'→'serie_b', 'Serie C'→'serie_c', 'Copa do Brasil'→'copa_do_brasil'.\n- league: find fixture by (comp, season, home_key, away_key): \n  - exists & played → attach stats (if none yet, or better match)\n  - exists & unplayed → fill goals + date (keep existing round_label) + stats\n  - absent → new Match (round_label None)\n- copa: fixtures list by (season, home_key, away_key):\n  - any played match → attach stats to best match (score-equal preferred)\n  - all unplayed (or NA rows) & brf played → fill first unplayed match (goals+date+stats); if multiple unplayed matches same key (2021 round 4 has both legs! e.g., (criciuma, fluminense, 2021) has 2 NA rows = 2 legs) → fill the ones... hmm: brf has 2 played rows for the tie (both legs, possibly SAME (pair,season) if same home team? no — legs alternate home: leg1 Criciúma home, leg2 Fluminense home → DIFFERENT keys ✓). So (pair, season) unplayed NA rows are 1 per leg-order ✓. Fill by matching pair order.\n  - absent → new Match (no round label)\n  \n  Wait — cup 2021 NA: rows are (Criciúma home, Fluminense away) and (Fluminense home, Criciúma away) — two DIFFERENT keys ✓. BR-Foot 2021 has both legs with respective home teams ✓ fills each ✓.\n\n- stats parsing: home_corner etc via to_int.\n\nSeason for BR-Foot: int(date[:4]).\n\n**Ordering issue**: BR-Foot copa rows for fixtures where cup file has the match PLAYED but with a different score (562/576 score sets matched; ~14 mismatch) → attach stats only if a stats row matches the score? If scores disagree, attaching stats from a mismatched row is wrong-ish; but could be a data error either way. Rule: attach stats from score-matching row; if none, attach from the row with closest date? Simpler: attach from score-matching row only; if none, attach the first one anyway with... no — keep it simple: prefer score-match; else attach closest-date row (data noise, best effort). Hmm, honestly simplest: prefer score match; else nearest date. I'll do that.\n\n**FIFA load**: rows → Player objects. club: raw or None if empty. Map clubs: `self.club_teams: dict[club_display, team_key|None]` built via registry resolution — but resolution can be ambiguous (\"Botafogo\" dominance rj ✓ auto). Use resolve(); matched → key. This powers players_by_club(brazilian_clubs_only) and cross-file enrichment (team_profile shows FIFA squad when team maps to a FIFA club).\n\n**Precomputed structures for service**:\n- matches list (all)\n- players list\n- registry\n- club→team_key map\n- per-competition seasons\n- notes dict\n\nLet me also prepare `SoccerData.summary()` for README/test counts.\n\n**Now the service layer** — signatures as planned. Let me write formatting utilities inside service.\n\nLet me write loader.py now. One subtle thing: `Match.home`/`away` are TeamRef(key, display). When registry display refreshes later (better variants registered), TeamRef.display could be stale. Solution: build Match objects AFT