tleticomg\") ✓ consistent (no dash!). My keys have no dash: \"atleticomg\", \"flamengorj\" — good, matches ALIASES values and derbies.py keys (\"flamengorj\" ✓, \"atleticopr\" ✓, \"saopaulosp\" ✓, \"palmeirassp\" ✓, \"corinthianssp\" ✓, \"gremiors\" ✓, \"internacionalrs\" ✓, \"bahiaba\" ✓, \"vitoriaba\" ✓, \"coritibapr\" ✓, \"vascorj\" ✓, \"botafogorj\" ✓, \"santossp\" ✓, \"fluminenserj\" ✓ — all consistent with fold(base+UF) no-dash ✓).\n\nAlso add ALIASES: \"vasco\" → \"vascorj\". And others where bare short names might appear in lib: \"Atletico Nacional\" (Colombian, lib 2016!) — \"Atlético Nacional\" appears in lib (final 2016!). base fold \"atleticonacional\" → no alias → new entity \"atleticonacional\" ✓ distinct ✓. \"Nacional (PAR)\" → nacionalpar ✓ distinct from nacionaluru ✓. \"Barcelona-EQU\" → barcelonaequ. Also \"The Strongest\", \"Toluca\" etc. — plain entities ✓.\n\nOne more check — lib bare \"Flamengo\" (2019-2021 rows) → dominance → flamengorj ✓. lib \"Athletico\"?? The NA row: \"Athletico\" bare! → fold \"athletico\"→\"atletico\" → base \"atletico\" ambiguous {mg, pr, go, ba, es, ac} → NO dominance → register creates NEW entity \"atletico\" (separate!). Then my 2022-final fixup must map it to atleticopr explicitly. Since the fixup row is Flamengo vs Athletico — I'll hard-map \"athletico\" → atleticopr in the fixup (the 2022 finalist). But wait — does bare \"Athletico\" appear elsewhere in lib (2022 semis: Athletico vs Palmeiras — spelled \"Athletico\"?). If lib 2022 rows spell it \"Athletico\" bare, they'd all become the orphan \"atletico\" entity — breaking queries. Let me handle via alias: add ALIASES[\"atletico\"]... no — \"atletico\" ambiguous, can't alias globally. Add alias \"athletico\"→atleticopr? fold(\"athletico\") = \"atletico\" — SAME fold! Aliases are keyed by fold — collision with the ambiguous base. Hmm. But ALIASES lookup happens BEFORE unique/dominance in my register order? Let me set: stateless resolution order: ALIASES → unique → 