ed":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788241902698,"end":1788241902701}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Lib file has bare names: \"Palmeiras\", \"Corinthians\", \"Fluminense\", \"Botafogo\", \"Cruzeiro\", \"Flamengo\", \"Internacional\", \"Santos\", \"Vasco\", \"Athletico\".\n\n- \"Palmeiras\" → unique base → palmeirassp ✓\n- \"Corinthians\" → unique → corinthianssp ✓\n- \"Fluminense\" → unique ✓\n- \"Botafogo\" → dominance → botafogorj ✓ (lib Botafogo = RJ ✓)\n- \"Cruzeiro\" → unique → cruzeiromg ✓\n- \"Flamengo\" → dominance → flamengorj ✓\n- \"Internacional\" → dominance → internacionalrs ✓\n- \"Santos\" → dominance → santossp ✓ (lib Santos = SP ✓ — Santos Laguna is Mexican, different base \"santoslaguna\" ✓)\n- \"Vasco\" → need alias \"vasco\" → vascorj ✓ (add to ALIASES)\n- \"Athletico\" → fold \"atletico\" → ambiguous, no dominance → orphan entity! Add lib-specific fixup: in the lib loader, map raw name \"Athletico\" → \"Athletico-PR\" before registration. All 29 occurrences are Atlético-PR (who played lib 2019? no... Athletico-PR won Copa Sudamericana 2018 & played lib 2019? and 2022 run to final ✓ + group stages 2020? 29 occurrences ≈ 2022 campaign (8 group + ... ) + others. All the same club ✓).\n\nAlso \"Gremio\" bare in lib? It showed 'Gremio-RS' in my test tuple but output has no Gremio line — wait, output shows no 'Gremio'... The filter included 'Gremio' prefix — no matches?? Odd — Grêmio played lib 2017 (champion!). The output doesn't show Gremio at all — maybe spelled \"Grêmio\" (accent) — my startswith('Gremio') fails on 'Grêmio' ✓ that's why. Fine — \"Grêmio\" → unique base \"gremio\" → gremiors ✓.\n\nAlso earlier collision list showed lib's \"Nacional (URU)\" and \"Barcelona-EQU\" ✓ handled.\n\nNow write the loader.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b85e319001e8qYu9V2W4Jd7I","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b85b87d001sFr7EiUqeRy