season) + 111 (2020 tail)**. 380+111 = 491 ✓ PERFECT. After season fix, brf 2021-bucket rows split 111→2020, 380→2021 ✓. And 2020 bucket: 264+111 = 375 ≈ 380 (5 missing? the \"vascodagama: 6, botafogo: 5...\" home counts are for 2021-bucket rows = 2020-tail matches ✓). Hmm 264+111=375 vs 380 — 5 short, whatever (brf is incomplete for 2020 early rounds — those br-file rows exist with scores ✓ no data loss overall).\n\nTHIRD issue: **atleticogoianiense / ecbahia / fortalezafc / operariofc / bragantino** key mismatches (the parse_name decorative bug + missing aliases). After the decorative fix: \"EC Bahia\" → bahiaba ✓, \"Fortaleza FC\" → fortalezace ✓, \"Operario FC MS\" → operarioms ✓. Remaining mismatches needing aliases:\n- \"Atletico Goianiense\" → atleticogo (BR-Foot spells full name; br file \"Atletico-GO\").\n- \"Macae Esporte\" → macae?? does cup have \"Macaé\"? Let me check cup bases for macae... I'll write a diagnostic after fixes listing brf bases with zero cross-source presence, then curate.\n- \"Metropolitano Maringa\" vs cup \"Maringá - PR\"?? different clubs? Metropolitano-Maringá... it IS from Maringá — club \"Metropolitano\" (SC)?? no — \"Metropolitano\" is a Santa Catarina club... but this says PR. Leave as-is (orphan, tiny).\n- \"Athletic Club MG\" — Athletic Club (MG) real club (Série C 2022+) — cup \"Athletic - MG\"? maybe exists ✓ check.\n- \"Duque De Caxias RJ\" → duquedecaxias ✓ = cup \"Duque de Caxias - RJ\" ✓ consistent already.\n- \"Uniclinic CE\" → vs cup \"Uniclínic\"? hmm \"Uniclinic\" vs \"Uniclínic\" — fold equal ✓ if cup has it. \n- \"Independente PA\" vs cup \"Independente - PA\" ✓.\n- \"Penarol AM\" vs cup \"Peñarol - AM\"? fold(\"Peñarol\")=\"penarol\" ✓ match.\n\nSo the systematic orphans after the fix: atleticogoianiense, macaeesporte, metropolitanomaringa, athleticclub... Let me also reconsider \"Sport Recife\" — wait brf spells \"Sport Recife\"?? From the parse list: I saw `raw='Sao Francisco PA'` etc. but not \"Sport Recife\" — earlier diagnostic showed 'sportrecife' as a base in brf 2021 (\"sportrecife\": 25). So brf also has \"Sport Recife\" spelling! base \"sportrecife\" ≠ \"sport\" → orphan for Sport-PE!! My ALIASES has fold(\"Sport Recife\") → \"sportpe\" ✓ — the alias IS there ✓ (base stateless → ALIASES lookup → sportpe ✓ good).\n\nAnd \"Atletico Mineiro\" → alias ✓. \"Athletico Paranaense\"/\"Atletico Paranaense\" → alias ✓.\n\nSo remaining curated aliases needed: atleticogoianiense → atleticogo, macaeesporte → macaerj?? (Macaé is RJ — cup \"Macaé - RJ\"? need to check). Let me run the orphan diagnostic after fixing parse_name.\n\nFOURTH issue — **serie B/C join key must include date** (legit same-pair-same-season twice, e.g. Serie C group+knockout). Change: for serie_b/serie_c (BR-Foot only sources), key = (comp, season, home, away, date). But wait — brf internal EXACT dupes (same date+pair) — none (dated-dupes: 0) ✓. So key with date keeps everything and loses nothing. But then _merge_extended lookup for leagues uses (comp, season, home, away) — for serie_b/c I must use the dated key. Implement: league fixture key = (comp, season, home, away) for brasileirao (sources agree; round-robin unique) and (comp, season, home, away, date) for serie_b/c. In _merge_extended: build lookup key accordingly. Hmm — but a postponed-match date typo between... brf is the ONLY source for b/c → no cross-source date mismatch ✓ exact-dated key is safe.\n\nHmm — wait, actually is it? Serie B 2021 dupes like (csa, brasildepelotas) twice same season — different dates — are those TWO real matches? Serie B 2021: CSA vs Brasil de Pelotas home-and-away = (csa, brasildepelotas) ONCE + (brasildepelotas, csa) once. Same order twice = one is likely a DATA ERROR (duplicate entry with wrong date) OR a replayed match. Hmm. If data error, keeping both double-counts standings; dropping loses nothing real. Can't know. 37 in serie B, 74 in serie C over 10 seasons — I'll keep both (dated key) and note in README that BR-Foot Serie B/C contains a small number of same-fixture entries which are kept as recorded. Meh — but standings for serie B could be slightly off... Alternatively dedupe serie_b/c by (pair, season) preferring first: loses the Serie C group+knockout legit repeats. Decision: dated key (keep everything). Actually hmm — let me quickly check a Serie C 2023 case: (brusque, amazonas) twice. Serie C 2023 format: 20 teams... group stage single round-robin (19 matches) + second phase groups of 4 (double round-robin?? no—). Second phase: 4 groups of 4, home-and-away within group → pairs meet twice (both orders) → (brusque, amazonas) could occur in group stage AND second phase same order if both advanced in same group! ✓ LEGIT. So dated-key is correct for Serie C. For Serie B — the dupes might be errors, but keeping is the safer default (they have scores; probably replays/abandoned-then-replayed). Go with dated key for b/c.\n\nFIFTH issue — the `_competition` valid-id-vs-error bug. Refactor to return (comp_id, error).\n\nSIXTH — finalize_displays + refresh TeamRef displays after loading.\n\nSEVENTH — derbies.py keys: \"vascorj\" → \"vascodagamarj\". Check all derby keys against registry: flamengorj ✓, fluminenserj ✓, botafogorj ✓, vascodagamarj (fix), corinthianssp ✓, palmeirassp ✓, saopaulosp ✓, gremiors ✓, internacionalrs ✓, bahiaba ✓, vitoriaba ✓, atleticopr ✓, coritibapr ✓, santossp ✓.\n\nAlso ALIASES: \"Vasco\" → vascodagamarj; \"Vasco da Gama\" → vascodagamarj.\n\nLet me now also double-check \"Internacional SC\" (brf \"EC Internacional SC\") — after decorative fix → base \"internacional\" + SC → internacionalsc ✓ = cup \"Internacional - SC\" ✓.\n\nAnd check brf \"Santos AP\" → santosap — cup has \"Santos - AP\" ✓ consistent — small Amapá club ✓ separate from santossp ✓.\n\nNow — implement all fixes:\n\n1. parse_name: base = fold(stripped name).\n2. ALIASES: fix Vasco entries; add atleticogoianiense; run orphan diagnostic for more.\n3. SUFFIX_ALIASES for (bragantino, SP) → redbullbragantinosp.\n4. BR-Foot season rules: leagues month≤2 → year-1; copa (year==2021 and month≤4) → 2020.\n5. League fixture keys: dated for serie_b/c.\n6. _competition refactor.\n7. finalize_displays + refresh.\n8. derbies key fix.\n\nLet me write these changes now. First normalize.py fixes:","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b8f4ff1001sIYvTWhxgTDAAj","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b8e280c001Zb7Tb6oHlB27lN"}}
