{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788242566439,"sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b8af9bedc688300b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","newString":"    def _add(self, match: Match) -> Match:\n        self.matches.append(match)\n        if match.competition in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\") and match.season:\n            self._league_fixtures[self._league_key(match)] = match\n        elif match.competition == \"copa_do_brasil\" and match.season:\n            self._cup_fixtures[\n                (match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n            ].append(match)\n        return match\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _league_key(match: Match):\n        \"\"\"Fixture identity within a league season.\n\n        Serie A is a pure double round-robin: one fixture per ordered pair,\n        so the pair alone identifies it (sources may disagree on dates).\n        Serie B/C data comes from a single source that also contains group\n        stages, where the same ordered pair legitimately meets twice in one\n        season, so the date is part of the key there.\n        \"\"\"\n        if match.competition == \"brasileirao\":\n            return (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n        return (\n            match.competition,\n            match.season,\n            match.home.key,\n            match.away.key,\n            match.date,\n        )\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _brf_season(comp_id: str, when) -> int | None:\n        \"\"\"Infer the season of a BR-Football row from its date.\n\n        Brazilian leagues run April-December, so January/February league\n        matches belong to the previous season (the COVID-delayed 2020\n        Serie A/B/C ran into Jan/Feb 2021). The 2020 Copa do Brasil\n        similarly finished in March/April 2021.\n        \"\"\"\n        if when is None:\n            return None\n        year = when.year\n        if comp_id in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\"):\n            return year - 1 if when.month <= 2 else year\n        if year == 2021 and when.month <= 4:\n            return 2020\n        return year","oldString":"    def _add(self, match: Match) -> Match:\n        self.matches.append(match)\n        if match.competition in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\") and match.season:\n            self._league_fixtures[\n                (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n            ] = match\n        elif match.competition == \"copa_do_brasil\" and match.season:\n            self._cup_fixtures[\n                (match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n            ].append(match)\n        return match"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -150,17 +150,53 @@\n \n def _add(self, match: Match) -> Match:\n     self.matches.append(match)\n     if match.competition in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\") and match.season:\n-        self._league_fixtures[\n-            (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n-        ] = match\n+        self._league_fixtures[self._league_key(match)] = match\n     elif match.competition == \"copa_do_brasil\" and match.season:\n         self._cup_fixtures[\n             (match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n         ].append(match)\n     return match\n \n+@staticmethod\n+def _league_key(match: Match):\n+    \"\"\"Fixture identity within a league season.\n+\n+    Serie A is a pure double round-robin: one fixture per ordered pair,\n+    so the pair alone identifies it (sources may disagree on dates).\n+    Serie B/C data comes from a single source that also contains group\n+    stages, where the same ordered pair legitimately meets twice in one\n+    season, so the date is part of the key there.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if match.competition == \"brasileirao\":\n+        return (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n+    return (\n+        match.competition,\n+        match.season,\n+        match.home.key,\n+        match.away.key,\n+        match.date,\n+    )\n+\n+@staticmethod\n+def _brf_season(comp_id: str, when) -> int | None:\n+    \"\"\"Infer the season of a BR-Football row from its date.\n+\n+    Brazilian leagues run April-December, so January/February league\n+    matches belong to the previous season (the COVID-delayed 2020\n+    Serie A/B/C ran into Jan/Feb 2021). The 2020 Copa do Brasil\n+    similarly finished in March/April 2021.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if when is None:\n+        return None\n+    year = when.year\n+    if comp_id in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\"):\n+        return year - 1 if when.month <= 2 else year\n+    if year == 2021 and when.month <= 4:\n+        return 2020\n+    return year\n+\n def _build_matches(self) -> None:\n     self._build_brasileirao()\n     self._build_historical_brasileirao()\n     self._build_copa_do_brasil()\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-x26yewvv/retort-d2915a49bf69/brazilian_soccer/loader.py\n@@ -150,17 +150,53 @@\n \n def _add(self, match: Match) -> Match:\n     self.matches.append(match)\n     if match.competition in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\") and match.season:\n-        self._league_fixtures[\n-            (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n-        ] = match\n+        self._league_fixtures[self._league_key(match)] = match\n     elif match.competition == \"copa_do_brasil\" and match.season:\n         self._cup_fixtures[\n             (match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n         ].append(match)\n     return match\n \n+@staticmethod\n+def _league_key(match: Match):\n+    \"\"\"Fixture identity within a league season.\n+\n+    Serie A is a pure double round-robin: one fixture per ordered pair,\n+    so the pair alone identifies it (sources may disagree on dates).\n+    Serie B/C data comes from a single source that also contains group\n+    stages, where the same ordered pair legitimately meets twice in one\n+    season, so the date is part of the key there.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if match.competition == \"brasileirao\":\n+        return (match.competition, match.season, match.home.key, match.away.key)\n+    return (\n+        match.competition,\n+        match.season,\n+        match.home.key,\n+        match.away.key,\n+        match.date,\n+    )\n+\n+@staticmethod\n+def _brf_season(comp_id: str, when) -> int | None:\n+    \"\"\"Infer the season of a BR-Football row from its date.\n+\n+    Brazilian leagues run April-December, so January/February league\n+    matches belong to the previous season (the COVID-delayed 2020\n+    Serie A/B/C ran into Jan/Feb 2021). The 2020 Copa do Brasil\n+    similarly finished in March/April 2021.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if when is None:\n+        return None\n+    year = when.year\n+    if comp_id in (\"brasileirao\", \"serie_b\", \"serie_c\"):\n+        return year - 1 if when.month <= 2 else year\n+    if year == 2021 and when.month <= 4:\n+        return 2020\n+    return year\n+\n def _build_matches(self) -> None:\n     self._build_brasileirao()\n     self._build_historical_brasileirao()\n     self._build_copa_do_brasil()\n","additions":39,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/loader.py","time":{"start":1788242566436,"end":1788242566438}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now fix the loader:\n1. BR-Foot season assignment (leagues: month≤2 → year-1; copa: 2021 months 1-4 → 2020).\n2. League fixture keys: dated for serie_b/c.\n3. finalize_displays + refresh TeamRefs.\n4. _competition refactor in service.py.\n\nFor the loader league fixture key — I'll keep `_league_fixtures` keyed by (comp, season, home, away) for brasileirao AND (comp, season, home, away, date) for serie_b/c? Two dicts is cleaner: `_league_fixtures` (brasileirao, pair-keyed) and `_brf_league_fixtures` (serie_b/c, date-keyed). Actually simpler: single dict but key includes date only for b/c:\n\n```python\ndef _league_key(self, comp_id, season, home_key, away_key, when):\n    if comp_id == 'brasileirao':\n        return (comp_id, season, home_key, away_key)\n    return (comp_id, season, home_key, away_key, when)\n```\nAnd _add computes it; _merge_extended computes it. For _merge_extended on brasileirao, the lookup key needs no date — but I have `when` anyway; just call _league_key. Wait — for brasileirao the lookup MUST be date-less (sources disagree on dates; round-robin uniqueness guarantees identity). For serie_b/c date must match exactly (same source only). ✓ this design works.\n\nEdge: brf serie_b row whose (pair, season, date) key already exists → enrich (dedupe exact repeats) ✓.\n\nAlso for season assignment: compute in _build_extended_stats:\n\n```python\ndef _brf_season(self, comp_id, when: date) -> int | None:\n    if when is None: return None\n    year = when.year\n    if comp_id in ('brasileirao','serie_b','serie_c'):\n        return year - 1 if when.month <= 2 else year\n    # Copa do Brasil: the 2020 edition ran into March/April 2021\n    if year == 2021 and when.month <= 4:\n        return 2020\n    return year\n```\n\nHmm wait — actually also check: are there brf COPA rows in Jan/Feb of OTHER years that belong to that same year (normal copa first rounds in Feb)? 2022 copa first round: Feb 22? 2023 copa: Feb 21? So Feb 2022/2023 → same year ✓ handled (only 2021 special-cased). But careful — 2020 copa: rounds 1-3 played Jan-Mar 2020?? Hmm — 2020 Copa first rounds: Jan 22-Feb 13 2020 ✓ same-year ✓ fine.\n\nAnd what about copa rows in month 5-12 of 2021 — the 2021 copa ran May-Dec ✓ year 2021 ✓.\n\n3. After _build_matches: \n```python\nself.registry.finalize_displays()\nfor m in self.matches:\n    m.home = TeamRef(m.home.key, self.registry.display(m.home.key))\n    m.away = TeamRef(m.away.key, self.registry.display(m.away.key))\n```\nTeamRef is frozen dataclass — replace instances ✓.\n\nWait — also _ref() calls registry.register(count_appearance=False) during Phase 2 — register calls note_variant + refresh_display — refresh_display will RE-PICK a suffixed variant after finalize? finalize runs AFTER _build_matches ✓ no registrations after that except... _load_players → club_team_key → registry.resolve (no registration) ✓. But refresh_display inside register during phase 2 — fine, finalize comes later ✓. But wait — finalize_displays picks bare display; then if someone registers later, refresh_display would override. No registrations after finalize ✓. Also refresh_display picks max by (accent, has_state, -length) — prefers suffixed! So if any registration happened post-finalize it'd revert. Not an issue in practice.\n\nAlso — `_bare_variant` checks `team.state.lower() in fold(variant)[-2:]` — e.g. variant \"Flamengo\" fold \"flamengo\"[-2:] = \"go\" ≠ \"rj\" ✓ bare kept. Variant \"Flamengo-RJ\" fold \"flamengorj\"[-2:] = \"rj\" ✓ suffixed skipped. For Botafogo-RJ variants: \"Botafogo RJ\" fold \"botafogorj\" ✓ skip; \"Botafogo\" (novo? brf?) → bare ✓. Good. But hmm — variants like \"Grêmio\" fold \"gremio\"[-2:]=\"io\" ≠ \"rs\" ✓. Careful false-positive: a variant whose fold ENDs with the state letters by coincidence, e.g. team \"Santa Cruz-PE\", variant \"Santa Cruz\" fold \"santacruz\"[-2:]=\"uz\" ≠ \"pe\" ✓. Team \"Ceará-CE\" bare \"Ceará\" fold \"ceara\"[-2:]=\"ra\" ≠ \"ce\" ✓. OK.\n\nEdge: `_bare_variant` for Atlético-GO... not dominant → never called ✓.\n\n4. service._competition refactor → return tuple. Update call sites: _filter_matches, team_stats, league_standings, finals, biggest_wins, competition_info, search... Let me rewrite those parts.\n\nAlso — while at it, `_pick_stats_target` uses `.toordinal()` on `m.date or when` — if m.date None and when None → crash; when is always a date there (BR-Foot rows have dates) ✓. But `min(played, key=...)` — if all dates None → fallback fine.\n\nAlso in `search_matches` the subject line: `COMPETITIONS[resolve_competition(competition) or \"brasileirao\"]` — fine after refactor.\n\nLet me now patch loader.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b9001be001Afff2jQ7SzB3sO","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b8fb328001YZ3f4YUZMuOoWX"}}
