to Santo club is \"Vitória\"?? no... The famous Vitória is Salvador-BA. There's \"Vitória da Conquista\" (different base). Hmm, no significant \"Vitória-ES\" club exists in these datasets — brf \"Vitoria ES\" — is that ALSO Vitória-BA mislabeled?! brf has \"Vitoria ES\" (from parse list) — 2014 Serie A Vitória-BA = brf \"Vitoria ES\"?? So brf ALSO labels Vitória(-BA) as ES?! Bizarre — maybe both Kaggle datasets share the error. OR brf \"Vitoria ES\" really means Vitória-BA (they play Serie A 2014-2015...). Since br 2014 has complete Vitória-BA fixtures under vitoriaba, the brf \"Vitoria ES\" rows FAILED to join → created vitoriaes 2014 dupes.\n\nSo: SUFFIX_ALIASES[(\"vitoria\",\"es\")] → \"vitoriaba\" merges novo's home rows AND brf's \"Vitoria ES\" rows into vitoriaba ✓. Then novo Vitória home (ES→vitoriaba ✓) and away (BA→vitoriaba ✓) unify ✓. brf \"Vitoria ES\" → vitoriaba → joins br fixtures ✓ (score check: brf 2014 Vitória vs br — agree? presumably ✓ same as other teams).\n\nBut CAREFUL: does brf have a REAL Vitória-ES club anywhere (Serie C/D)? If brf Serie C had the actual ES club... The parse list showed only 'Vitoria ES'. And bare \"Vitoria\" (393 matches — copa from brf: \"Vitoria\" stateless → candidates {vitoriaba, vitoriaes-after-fix?...} hmm). After the suffix alias, _by_base[\"vitoria\"] = {vitoriaba} only?? — then stateless \"Vitoria\" → unique → vitoriaba ✓ ALL merge into vitoriaba ✓. The 393 bare-vitoria matches (mostly brf copa 2021-2023 + serie B 2021?? Vitória-BA in serie B 2021-2022 ✓ copa 2022-2023 ✓) → vitoriaba ✓ correct (Vitória-BA played those).\n\nWait — but the copa joins: brf copa \"Vitoria\" rows (2022-2023) — cup file has no 2022-2023 → new matches ✓ fine either way.\n\nAlso — `vitoriaes` in serie A 2013 with 19 matches: novo 2013 Vitória home games (Serie A 2013 — wait Vitória WAS in Serie A 2013? br file 2013 shows Vitoria-BA ✓ yes promoted). novo 2013 Vitória home → ES → vitoriaes; br 2013 → vitoriaba → BOTH exist → +19 dupes ✓ explained. After fix: novo 2013 Vitória home → vitoriaba → dedupe skip ✓ 380 ✓.\n\nNow the remaining odd counts in 2014: `vitoria` bare 28 — brf stateless \"Vitoria\" rows in Serie A 2014?? 28 — hmm whatever — after fix → unique candidate vitoriaba → join br fixtures ✓.\n\nAnd 2022's +38: teams with 40 counts — hmm 2022: all teams 40 instead of 38?! 40 = 38 + 2 → TWO extra matches per team?? 418 = 380+38 — if distributed 2 per team across 19 teams... hmm actually teams listed at 40: fluminense, santos, atleticogo, flamengo, palmeiras, ceara, coritiba, goias, atleticomg, internacionalrs, botafogorj, corinthianssp, fortalezace, cuiabamt, avai, americamg, saopaulosp, atleticopr, juventuders — 19 teams × 40 = but wait that counts appearances; extra 38 matches ≈ each involving 2 teams → total extra appearances 76 / 19 teams = 4?? Confusing. The 20th team (not listed) has 38. Hmm — 19 teams at 40 → sum = 19×40+38 = 798 appearances = 399 matches?? But season shows 418. Ugh, whatever — 2022 brf = 379 rows: joins for played br fixtures; br 2022 rounds 31-38 = 81 NA rows (unplayed) → brf fills them; 379 − 380 = −1... Hmm 418 = 380 br + 38 brf-new. 38 brf-new = brf rows that didn't join. Which? Atletico-GO rows?? — atleticogo at 40 (2 extra). Maybe name mismatches remain for SOME teams in SOME seasons (e.g. \"Juventude\" vs novo \"Juventude-RS\"?? br 2022 \"Juventude-RJ\"?? no — Juventude-RS... let me just diagnose 2022 brf-new matches directly — which pairs failed.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05b935074001de8V02fsZqe0eF","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","messageID":"msg_05b92f8d2001w25IoKH0QdRu1M"}}
