{"type":"text","timestamp":1788244122680,"sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","part":{"id":"prt_05ba7bf6b001RDdHO0FP9xnzfn","messageID":"msg_05ba79d7a001CjEWAFR4YNXK5k","sessionID":"ses_fa4885bb0ffe9T9m197C2RPPvh","type":"text","text":"All 120 tests pass, pyflakes clean, server verified over the MCP protocol. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server per TASK.md:\n\n**Server** — `server.py` (MCP 2.x SDK, stdio transport) exposing 11 tools: `search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `team_stats`, `team_profile`, `league_standings`, `finals`, `biggest_wins`, `competition_info`, `search_players`, `players_by_club`, `derby_matches`.\n\n**Package** — `brazilian_soccer/`:\n- `normalize.py` — accent/case-insensitive folding, state-suffix parsing (`Palmeiras-SP` / `Palmeiras - SP` / `Botafogo RJ`), curated aliases (`Atletico Mineiro` → Atlético-MG), dominance-based disambiguation (bare `Flamengo` → RJ, bare `Atletico` → candidate list), all 3 dataset date formats\n- `loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into one graph with cross-file dedup/enrichment: the two Brasileirão files merged (2012–2019 overlap dropped), extended stats attached as corners/shots/attacks, unplayed 2022 rounds filled, 2023 season and Serie B/C added, COVID-calendar season correction (Jan/Feb matches → previous season), cup finals stamped, plus fixes for source data errors (Vitória-BA mislabeled ES, split Vasco/Bragantino/Atlético-GO entities, one junk row)\n- `service.py` — all 5 required capability categories, formatted like the spec's example answers\n\n**Verified data integrity**: 2019 standings reproduce the spec's reference exactly (Flamengo 90 pts, 28W/6D/4L; Santos/Palmeiras 74); 2020/2022 champions and relegations match official history; every Serie A season 2006–2022 is exactly 380 matches after dedup.\n\n**Tests** — `tests/` with BDD Given/When/Then suites: 120 passing, covering match/team/player/competition/statistics queries, 24 sample questions from the spec, normalization edge cases, dedup invariants, UTF-8 handling, and a live end-to-end MCP stdio integration test.\n\n**Performance**: graph loads in ~1.3 s; simple lookups < 20 ms, heaviest aggregate 0.3 s (spec budget: 2 s / 5 s).","time":{"start":1788244115307,"end":1788244122675}}}
